<main class="write-main"><h1>Foundation access</h1><p>Invite a learner through Waithaka Ndegwa’s approved Ubunifu Foundation allocation. Ubunifu manages the learner account, required registration details and course access.</p><p><a class="wbtn primary" href="https://www.ubunifuinstitute.com/uims/foundation-access.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Ubunifu Foundation access ↗</a></p><h2>Create a private invitation</h2><ol><li>Sign in to Ubunifu with your authorised issuer account.</li><li>Select the approved allocation listed under Waithaka Ndegwa.</li><li>Enter the intended learner’s email and generate a single-use pass.</li><li>Copy the private invitation link or choose Ubunifu’s invitation email option.</li><li>The recipient completes their required details in Ubunifu. An existing learner must sign in with the matching account.</li></ol><h2>If no allocation appears</h2><p>An Ubunifu administrator must bind an existing approved Foundation allocation to Waithaka Ndegwa and grant your account issuer access. Being listed as an issuer does not itself provide places or permissions.</p><h2>Keep invitations private</h2><p>Passes are email-bound and expire within seven days or earlier if the allocation ends. Revoke unused invitations in Ubunifu when needed. Do not publish invitation links, learner details or codes on this website.</p><p>Goblis Foundation, Afribiz Consultancy and Afrisol Technologies use their own authorised allocations in the same Ubunifu workspace. This page does not transfer learner information or create an allocation.</p></main>
